.TH NEWUSER 8
.SH NAME
newuser \- create a user home directory from the shipped skeleton
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B newuser
[
.B -s
.I skeleton
]
.I name
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Newuser
creates
.BI /usr/ name
by copying the skeleton home directory (default
.BR /usr/inferno ),
then ensures the per-user working directories
.BR tmp ,
.B keyring
and
.B charon
exist.
The contents of the skeleton's
.B secstore
and
.B tmp
directories are not copied \(em credentials and temporary state are
per-user, never inherited.
.PP
On hosted installs the whole of
.B /usr
is durable (bound from
.BR ~/.infernode/usr ;
see
.BR /doc/PERSISTENCE.md ),
so the new home survives system updates by construction.
.PP
Creating the home does not grant network authentication: an
administrator adds the account on the signer with
.IR changelogin (8),
and the user obtains certificates at first login with
.IR getauthinfo (8),
exactly as in original Inferno.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/newuser.b
.SH HISTORY
Original Inferno documented this operation as prose \(em
.I "copy the directory /usr/inferno into /usr/username"
\(em and
.IR kfscmd (8)'s
.B newuser
command was documented inside a roff ignore-block but never
implemented. This command finishes that arc.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR logon (1),
.IR changelogin (8),
.IR getauthinfo (8)
